WEBVTT

NOTE Birch & Co and Cobalt Freight, northern lane. Tuesday 22 September 2026. Speakers: Iris Bell, Marta Quill, Sam Rivera.

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:09.000
<v Iris Bell>Marta, thanks. We're looking at shipping into the Nordics from next spring, and Sam is helping us choose a carrier.

00:00:09.500 --> 00:00:17.000
<v Marta Quill>Happy to help. Our northern lane runs three times a week, cross-dock in the south of Sweden, onward by partner.

00:00:17.500 --> 00:00:22.000
<v Sam Rivera>What would a rate look like for Birch, per pallet?

00:00:22.500 --> 00:00:31.000
<v Marta Quill>For your volumes, a hundred and forty-two euros a pallet, door to door. And we can take you from March.

00:00:31.500 --> 00:00:36.000
<v Iris Bell>From March. Not earlier?

00:00:36.500 --> 00:00:42.000
<v Marta Quill>March is what I can promise. I'd rather promise March and keep it.

00:00:42.500 --> 00:00:48.000
<v Iris Bell>And fuel? A fixed surcharge, or an index?

00:00:48.500 --> 00:00:55.000
<v Marta Quill>Index-linked, reviewed quarterly, both ways. Same terms as everyone.

00:00:55.500 --> 00:01:04.000
<v Marta Quill>To hold space for March I need a volume forecast by the second of October. Pallets per month, first six months.

00:01:04.500 --> 00:01:11.000
<v Sam Rivera>Iris, can you confirm the numbers to me by the thirtieth? I'll put the forecast together and send it to Marta.

00:01:11.500 --> 00:01:13.000
<v Iris Bell>The thirtieth, yes.

00:01:13.500 --> 00:01:19.000
<v Marta Quill>And I'll send the written quote by Friday, so you have it next to whoever else you're asking.
